From 91245bc1f11c1845c013d1e4996b2b083da67d3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Apr 2026 17:42:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] ktranslate-topology: add -demo flag with simulated
 enterprise topology
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a built-in demo seeder so the viewer can be exercised without
running SNMP against real gear. Pass -demo to seed a realistic
three-tier enterprise network and a goroutine refreshes the link
timestamps on a configurable interval (-demo-interval, default 10s)
so the viewer's auto-refresh clock stays live.

The fixture in demo.go defines 17 devices and 19 links:

  - 2 core routers (core-r1/r2) with an HSRP mesh
  - 3 distribution switches fully meshed to both cores
  - 6 access switches hanging off the distribution tier
  - 6 edge devices: two IP phones, two APs, a Linux server,
    a Windows workstation

Each device has a realistic Catalyst/ASR/AP sysDescr and a plausible
IP that show up in the node tooltips. Protocol coverage is mixed on
purpose so every colour of edge renders:

  - core mesh + core-to-dist: LLDP + CDP (blue, merged)
  - dist-to-access:           LLDP only (green)
  - phones, one AP:           CDP only (yellow)
  - one AP:                   LLDP + CDP (blue)

Each demoLink produces two Observations (one per endpoint) so the
graph store's reciprocal-view dedup path is exercised end-to-end —
38 observations collapse into 19 canonical edges.

Unit tests verify the seeded shape (17/19), that the lldp+cdp merge
lands on the expected link, that every interface is attached to a
real device parent, and that dist-to-access edges are lldp-only.

Usage:

  ./ktranslate-topology -listen :8082 -demo
  open http://localhost:8082/
